<span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mord vbox\"><span class=\"thinbox\"><span class=\"rlap\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"inner\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\"></span></span></span><span class=\"fix\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">250</span></span></span></span>","key":"gBnDnn9BTg"},{"type":"text","value":"), the p-value is the combination of the two tail areas: the area to the left of −2.5 plus the area to the right of 2.5.","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"gMRlftymhD"}],"key":"zZffTSJCbj"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The p-value is therefore 2 × P(Z > 2.5). We can either use a table or carry out the test using statistical software. In this case, we get a p-value of 0.012.","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"XdQYdUR54v"}],"key":"uFU2qTzcrQ"}],"class":"tip","key":"VjXZrJfCik"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Concept Check","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"JRRmaGB9hV"}],"identifier":"concept-check","label":"Concept Check","html_id":"concept-check","implicit":true,"key":"uB3mRQwm9S"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-c42528cfa98bfa4312e7267291d7fdee.mjs","model":{"question":"A z-test for μ with alternative Hₐ: μ < μ₀ produces z = −1.5. Which expression gives the p-value?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"P(Z ≤ −1.5)","feedback":"Correct! For a left-tailed test, the p-value is the area to the left of the observed test statistic: P(Z ≤ −1.5) ≈ 0.067."},{"correct":false,"text":"P(Z ≥ −1.5)","feedback":"The area to the right of −1.5 (≈ 0.933) would essentially measure agreement with H₀."},{"correct":false,"text":"2P(Z ≤ −1.5)","feedback":"Doubling is only for two-sided alternatives."}],"multi":false,"hint":"A \"less than\" alternative is left-tailed.","explanation":""},"key":"OtfNsnjJC9"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-c42528cfa98bfa4312e7267291d7fdee.mjs","model":{"question":"In example 2, the p-value was 0.012. Which is the correct interpretation?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"If μ were 250 ppm, the probability of a sample mean as far from 250 as 247 is (in either direction) would be 0.012","feedback":"Correct! If the mean concentration really were 250 ppm, there would be only a 0.012 probability of getting a sample mean at least 2.5 standard deviations away from 250 (in either direction)."},{"correct":false,"text":"There is a 1.2% chance that the mean concentration is 250 ppm","feedback":"The p-value is not the probability that H₀ is true."},{"correct":false,"text":"If μ were 250 ppm, the probability of a sample mean of 247 or lower would be 0.012","feedback":"Since the alternative is two-sided, \"as extreme\" includes both directions, not just below."}],"